# 高频词汇 List05
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List05核心词汇

{{range}}{/reɪndʒ/}{范围；山脉}{The product comes in a wide range of colors.}}
{{rational}}{/ˈræʃənl/}{理性的；合理的}{We need to make rational decisions based on facts.}}
{{recognize}}{/ˈrekəɡnaɪz/}{认出；承认}{The government recognized the need for reform.}}
{{recommend}}{/ˌrekəˈmend/}{推荐；建议}{I recommend this book to anyone interested in history.}}
{{reflect}}{/rɪˈflekt/}{反映；反思}{The data reflects a growing trend in online shopping.}}
{{reform}}{/rɪˈfɔːm/}{改革；改良}{The education reform aims to improve teaching quality.}}
{{regime}}{/reɪˈʒiːm/}{政权；体制}{The political regime underwent major changes.}}
{{region}}{/ˈriːdʒən/}{地区；区域}{This region is known for its rich cultural heritage.}}
{{regulate}}{/ˈreɡjuleɪt/}{管理；调节}{The government regulates the banking industry.}}
{{reject}}{/rɪˈdʒekt/}{拒绝；驳回}{The proposal was rejected by the committee.}}
{{relate}}{/rɪˈleɪt/}{联系；叙述}{How does this issue relate to our discussion?}}
{{release}}{/rɪˈliːs/}{释放；发布}{The company will release a new version next month.}}
{{relevant}}{/ˈreləvənt/}{相关的；切题的}{Please provide information relevant to the case.}}
{{relieve}}{/rɪˈliːv/}{缓解；减轻}{The medicine helped relieve the pain.}}
{{reluctant}}{/rɪˈlʌktənt/}{不情愿的；勉强的}{He was reluctant to admit his mistake.}}
{{rely}}{/rɪˈlaɪ/}{依赖；信赖}{Many students rely on scholarships to pay for college.}}
{{require}}{/rɪˈkwaɪər/}{要求；需要}{The position requires at least three years of experience.}}
{{research}}{/rɪˈsɜːtʃ/}{研究；调查}{Scientific research has led to many important discoveries.}}
{{resident}}{/ˈrezɪdənt/}{居民；住院医生}{The residents of this town are very friendly.}}
{{resist}}{/rɪˈzɪst/}{抵抗；抵制}{It is hard to resist the temptation of junk food.}}
{{resolve}}{/rɪˈzɒlv/}{解决；决心}{We need to resolve this conflict through dialogue.}}
{{resource}}{/rɪˈsɔːs/}{资源}{Natural resources must be used sustainably.}}
{{respond}}{/rɪˈspɒnd/}{回应；反应}{The company responded quickly to customer complaints.}}
{{restore}}{/rɪˈstɔːr/}{恢复；修复}{Efforts are underway to restore the historic building.}}
{{restrict}}{/rɪˈstrɪkt/}{限制；约束}{The new law restricts the sale of cigarettes to minors.}}
{{retain}}{/rɪˈteɪn/}{保留；保持}{The company struggles to retain talented employees.}}
{{reveal}}{/rɪˈviːl/}{揭示；透露}{The investigation revealed shocking details.}}
{{revenue}}{/ˈrevənjuː/}{收入；税收}{Government revenue has increased due to economic growth.}}
{{reverse}}{/rɪˈvɜːs/}{逆转；相反}{The trend has been reversed in recent years.}}
{{revolution}}{/ˌrevəˈluːʃn/}{革命；变革}{The digital revolution has transformed our lives.}
